![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The CLI script currently writes the drift snapshot to `clean-project-drift-snapshot.v1.json` but does not verify if the project is actually clean (`snapshot.clean === true`). If there is any drift or missing files, the script will silently exit with code `0`. To prevent silent failures in CI/CD pipelines, the script must explicitly fail closed and throw an error if drift or missing files are detected.

```javascript
if (command === 'snapshot' || command === 'all') {
  const snapshot = await buildDriftSnapshot(root, loaded);
  results.snapshot = await emit('clean-project-drift-snapshot.v1.json', snapshot);
  if (!snapshot.clean) {
    process.exitCode = 1;
    throw new Error(`Project drift detected! Match: ${snapshot.counts.match}, Drift: ${snapshot.counts.drift}, Missing: ${snapshot.counts.missing}`);
  }
}
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. CLI validation scripts must exit with a non-zero exit code for any validation status other than a successful pass (such as 'fail' or 'blocked') to prevent blocked or failed runs from passing silently in CI/CD pipelines.
</details>

