When validating expected array fields from upstream schemas or input data, explicitly verify that all expected elements are present (rather than just checking the array length) to prevent silent mismatches from renamed or replaced fields. If the field is present but is not an array, process it as an empty array and trigger a validation failure to ensure the system fails closed.

```javascript
const registryRows = Array.isArray(registry.registry) ? registry.registry : [];
const expectedRows = contract.registry.expected_rows || [];
const hasAllElements = expectedRows.every(item => registryRows.includes(item));
if (!Array.isArray(registry.registry) || !hasAllElements) {
  throw new Error('frozen registry shape mismatch');
}
